[22.392,"o","# Mission: Fix the misspelled hello-world greeting in hello.sh (parallix-adhoc-0001)\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\n`hello.sh` prints the greeting `Helo, Wrld!` — both words are misspelled. Correct the greeting so th \bat running `bash hello.sh` emits exactly `Hello, World!` followed by a single newline, with no other \b change to the script's behaviour, structure, or exit status (0).\r\n\r\n## Why Now\r\n`hello.sh` is the only executable artifact in this repository and is the canonical smoke target for  \bthe Parallix workflow demo. A visibly misspelled greeting makes the repo unusable as a reference exa \bmple, and any downstream demo, screenshot, or smoke assertion that quotes the expected output is wro \bng until the string is corrected. The defect is a two-character typo with no dependencies, so it can \b be closed in a single checkpoint rather than carried as open debt.\r\n\r\n## Refinement Signals\r\n- Predicted NEL bucket: Small (0–80)\r\n- Confidence: High\r\n- Selection note: activate as-is\r\n- Main drivers: single-file change to one `printf` stri"]
[25.392,"o","ng literal in `hello.sh`; no build system, no \b dependency graph, no test harness to extend; verification is a direct output comparison of `bash he \bllo.sh`\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\u001b[7mmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
