[43.506,"o"," succeeded in 0ms:\r\n.gitignore\r\nbacklog/tasks/parallix-adhoc-0001 - fix-hello-world-greeting.md\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md\r\nbacklog/tasks/parallix-adhoc-0001 - fix-hello-world-greeting.md:14:`hello.sh` prints the misspelled greeting `Helo, Wrld!`. Correct the `printf`\r\nbacklog/tasks/parallix-adhoc-0001 - fix-hello-world-greeting.md:18:Before: `printf \"Helo, Wrld!\\n\"`\r\nhello.sh:3:printf \"Helo, Wrld!\\n\"\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md:4:`hello.sh` prints the greeting `Helo, Wrld!` — both words are misspelled. Correct the greeting so that running `bash hello.sh` emits exactly `Hello, World!` followed by a single newline, with no other change to the script's behaviour, structure, or exit status (0).\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md:33:3. The strings `Helo` and `Wrld` no longer appear anywhere in the repository working tree — verifiable with `git grep -n -e Helo -e Wrld` returning no matches (exit status 1).\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md:40:- Assumption: the intended greeting is the conventional `Hello, World!` with a comma, a space, and a trailing exclamation mark. The backlog task says only \"fix hello world greeting\"; the misspellings `Helo`/`Wrld` make the intent unambiguous, and the file's own comment reads `# Hello world`.\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md:48:- CP 1: Correct the greeting string in `hello.sh` from `Helo, Wrld!` to `Hello, World!`, leaving the `# Hello world` comment, the blank line, and the `printf` form intact. Capture `bash hello.sh | od -c`, `git grep -n -e Helo -e Wrld` (expected: no match), and `git diff --stat` as evidence for criteria 1–5.\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md:57:  1. **Recognized repo commands or paths** — for this mission the durable forms are `` `bash hello.sh` ``, `` `bash hello.sh | od -c` ``, `` `git grep -n -e Helo -e Wrld` ``, `` `git diff --stat main...HEAD -- hello.sh` ``, `` `git diff --name-only main...HEAD` ``, `` `./scripts/verify-local.sh all` ``, and the path `hello.sh`\r\nmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md:70:| `Helo`/`Wrld` gone from the tree | `git grep -n -e Helo -e Wrld` exits 1 with no output | PASS |\r\nhello.sh\r\n\r\n"]
